IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XIV -- Financial Disclosure: the statements
-- (ss 155 to 160). The auditor (ss 161 to 172) is in cb3-part14-auditor.l4; Part XIV.1 (s 172.1) is in
-- cb3-part14-1-diversity.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. "Prescribed" financial statements and
-- requirements are plain BOOLEAN inputs, because the regulations are not a source. "Not less than twenty-one
-- days before" counts back from the meeting: the meeting day is day 0 and the twenty-first day before it is
-- in time, the mirror of the keel's convention for "within N days after" (fork F-159-before). Dates carry no
-- time of day. Dates: Part XIV holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XIV -- Financial Disclosure: the statements (ss 155 to 160)`

§§ `s 155 -- annual financial statements`

-- (1)(a)(i) The first set of comparative statements relates to the period that began on the date the corporation came into
-- existence and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting, or, if the corporation has completed a financial
-- year, the period that began immediately after the end of the last completed financial year and ended not more than six
-- months before the annual meeting. "Not more than six months before" is the keel's counting turned back: the period end is
-- day 0 and the meeting is in time on or after it and up to the last day of six months counted from it.
-- src:1930 | (i) the period that began on the date the corporation came into existence and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting or, if the corporation has completed a financial year, the period that began immediately after the end of the last completed financial year and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting, and
@ref CBCA s 155(1)(a)(i) (src:1930)
`the six months of s 155(1)(a)(i)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

@ref CBCA s 155(1)(a)(i) (src:1930)
GIVEN `the end of the last completed financial year, if the corporation has completed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the corporation came into existence` IS A DATE
      `the date the period began` IS A DATE
      `the date the period ended` IS A DATE
      `the date of the annual meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first period of the statements is as s 155(1)(a)(i) requires within s 155(1)(a)(i)` MEANS
        (CONSIDER `the end of the last completed financial year, if the corporation has completed one`
         WHEN JUST lastEnd THEN `the date the period began` EQUALS (lastEnd PLUS 1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the period began` EQUALS `the date the corporation came into existence`)
    AND `done within the time limit` `the six months of s 155(1)(a)(i)` `the date the period ended` `the date of the annual meeting`

-- (1)(a) The statements are prescribed comparative statements that conform to any prescribed requirements and relate
-- separately to (i) that period and (ii) the immediately preceding financial year. (2) The (ii) statements may be omitted if
-- the reason for the omission is set out in the financial statements, or in a note, to be placed before the shareholders.
-- src:1929 | (a) prescribed comparative financial statements that conform to any prescribed requirements and relate separately to
-- src:1930 | (i) the period that began on the date the corporation came into existence and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting or, if the corporation has completed a financial year, the period that began immediately after the end of the last completed financial year and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting, and
-- src:1931 | (ii) the immediately preceding financial year;
@ref CBCA s 155(1)(a) (src:1929-1931)
GIVEN `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statements placed are as s 155(1)(a) requires within s 155(1)(a)` MEANS
        `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements`
    AND `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)`
    AND (    `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year`
         OR  `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them`)

-- (1) The directors shall place before the shareholders at every annual meeting (a) those statements; (b) the report of the
-- auditor, if any; and (c) any further information respecting the financial position and results of operations required by the
-- articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement. The relation: the shareholders are owed the placing; the
-- directors owe it.
-- src:1928 | 155 (1) The directors of a corporation shall place before the shareholders at every annual meeting
-- src:1929 | (a) prescribed comparative financial statements that conform to any prescribed requirements and relate separately to
-- src:1930 | (i) the period that began on the date the corporation came into existence and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting or, if the corporation has completed a financial year, the period that began immediately after the end of the last completed financial year and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting, and
-- src:1931 | (ii) the immediately preceding financial year;
-- src:1932 | (b) the report of the auditor, if any; and
-- src:1933 | (c) any further information respecting the financial position of the corporation and the results of its operations required by the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 155(1) (src:1928-1933)
GIVEN `the statements placed are as s 155(1)(a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report of the auditor is placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement require further information respecting the financial position and results of operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that further information is placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors have complied with s 155(1) within s 155(1)` MEANS
        `the statements placed are as s 155(1)(a) requires`
    AND (    (NOT `the corporation has an auditor`)
         OR  `the report of the auditor is placed before the shareholders`)
    AND (    (NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement require further information respecting the financial position and results of operations`)
         OR  `that further information is placed before the shareholders`)

§§ `s 156 -- exemption`

-- On the application of a corporation, the Director may exempt it, on any terms the Director thinks fit, from any requirement
-- of s 155 or any of ss 157 to 160, if the Director reasonably believes that the detriment the requirement may cause the
-- corporation outweighs its benefit to the shareholders or, for a distributing corporation, to the public. The comparator is the
-- benefit to the shareholders for a corporation that is not distributing and to the public for one that is (fork F-156-public).
-- Whether the Director does exempt is the Director's discretion and is not decided.
-- src:1937 | 156 On the application of a corporation, the Director may exempt the corporation, on any terms that the Director thinks fit, from any requirement set out in section 155 or any of sections 157 to 160, if the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the shareholders or, in the case of a distributing corporation, to the public.
@ref CBCA s 156 (src:1937)
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is a requirement of section 155 or of any of sections 157 to 160` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may exempt the corporation within s 156` MEANS
        `the applicant is the corporation`
    AND `the requirement is a requirement of section 155 or of any of sections 157 to 160`
    AND (IF `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
         THEN `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the public`
         ELSE `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the shareholders`)

§§ `s 157 -- consolidated statements`

-- (1) A corporation shall keep at its registered office a copy of the financial statements of each of its subsidiary bodies
-- corporate and of each body corporate the accounts of which are consolidated in its own statements.
-- src:1939 | 157 (1) A corporation shall keep at its registered office a copy of the financial statements of each of its subsidiary bodies corporate and of each body corporate the accounts of which are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 157(1) (src:1939)
GIVEN `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must keep a copy of the statements within s 157(1)` MEANS
        `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation`
    OR  `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 157(1) (src:1939)
GIVEN `the corporation must keep a copy of the statements within s 157(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is kept at the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to keep a copy at the registered office is met within s 157(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must keep a copy of the statements within s 157(1)`)
    OR  `a copy is kept at the registered office of the corporation`

-- (2) Shareholders and their personal representatives may on request examine the statements during the usual business hours
-- of the corporation and make extracts free of charge, unless the court has barred the right under (3).
-- src:1941 | (2) Shareholders of a corporation and their personal representatives may on request examine the statements referred to in subsection (1) during the usual business hours of the corporation and may make extracts free of charge.
@ref CBCA s 157(2) (src:1941)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder or the personal representative of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person requests to examine the statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is during the usual business hours of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has barred the right of the person to examine under subsection 157(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder may examine the statements and make extracts free of charge within s 157(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder or the personal representative of a shareholder`
    AND `the person requests to examine the statements`
    AND `it is during the usual business hours of the corporation`
    AND (NOT `the court has barred the right of the person to examine under subsection 157(3)`)

-- (3) The corporation may, within fifteen days of a request to examine, apply to a court for an order barring the right of any
-- person to examine; the court may, if satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary
-- body corporate, bar the right and make any further order it thinks fit. The day of the request is day 0 and the fifteenth day
-- after it is in time (the keel's convention, fork F1).
-- src:1943 | (3) A corporation may, within fifteen days of a request to examine under subsection (2), apply to a court for an order barring the right of any person to so examine, and the court may, if it is satisfied that such examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate, bar such right and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 157(3) (src:1943)
`the fifteen days of s 157(3)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 157(3) (src:1943)
GIVEN `the date of the request to examine` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to bar the examination within s 157(3)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the fifteen days of s 157(3)` `counted from` `the date of the request to examine`

@ref CBCA s 157(3) (src:1943)
GIVEN `the date of the request to examine` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation applies to the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to the court within s 157(3)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the fifteen days of s 157(3)` `the date of the request to examine` `the date the corporation applies to the court`

@ref CBCA s 157(3) (src:1943)
GIVEN `the application was made within fifteen days of the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may bar the right to examine within s 157(3)` MEANS
        `the application was made within fifteen days of the request`
    AND `the court is satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate`

-- (4) The corporation shall give the Director and the person asking to examine notice of an application under (3), and the
-- Director and that person may appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
-- src:1945 | (4) A corporation shall give the Director and the person asking to examine under subsection (2) notice of an application under subsection (3), and the Director and such person may appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 157(4) (src:1945)
GIVEN `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must give notice of the application within s 157(4)` MEANS
    `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)`

@ref CBCA s 157(4) (src:1945)
GIVEN `the corporation must give notice of the application within s 157(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given to the person asking to examine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to give notice of the application is met within s 157(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must give notice of the application within s 157(4)`)
    OR  (    `notice was given to the Director`
         AND `notice was given to the person asking to examine`)

@ref CBCA s 157(4) (src:1945)
GIVEN `the person is the Director or the person asking to examine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director and the person may appear and be heard within s 157(4)` MEANS
    `the person is the Director or the person asking to examine`

§§ `s 158 -- approval of the financial statements`

-- (1) The directors shall approve the statements of s 155, the approval being evidenced by the manual signature of one or more
-- directors or a facsimile of the signatures reproduced in the statements.
-- src:1947 | 158 (1) The directors of a corporation shall approve the financial statements referred to in section 155 and the approval shall be evidenced by the manual signature of one or more directors or a facsimile of the signatures reproduced in the statements.
@ref CBCA s 158(1) (src:1947)
GIVEN `the number of directors who signed the statements manually` IS A NUMBER
      `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the approval is evidenced as s 158(1) requires within s 158(1)` MEANS
        `the number of directors who signed the statements manually` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements`

-- (2) A corporation shall not issue, publish or circulate copies of the statements unless they are (a) approved and signed in
-- accordance with (1); and (b) accompanied by the report of the auditor, if any. The first rule is the condition; the second says
-- the issuing is prohibited when the condition is not met.
-- src:1949 | (2) A corporation shall not issue, publish or circulate copies of the financial statements referred to in section 155 unless the financial statements are
-- src:1950 | (a) approved and signed in accordance with subsection (1); and
-- src:1951 | (b) accompanied by the report of the auditor of the corporation, if any.
@ref CBCA s 158(2) (src:1949-1951)
GIVEN `the statements are approved and signed in accordance with subsection 158(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are accompanied by the report of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the condition for issuing copies is met within s 158(2)` MEANS
        `the statements are approved and signed in accordance with subsection 158(1)`
    AND (    (NOT `the corporation has an auditor`)
         OR  `the statements are accompanied by the report of the auditor`)

@ref CBCA s 158(2) (src:1949-1951)
GIVEN `the corporation issues, publishes or circulates copies of the statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition for issuing copies is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`issuing copies is prohibited within s 158(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation issues, publishes or circulates copies of the statements`
    AND (NOT `the condition for issuing copies is met`)

§§ `s 159 -- copies to shareholders`

-- (1) A corporation shall, not less than twenty-one days before each annual meeting, or before the signing of a resolution under
-- s 142(1)(b) in lieu of the annual meeting, send a copy of the documents of s 155 to each shareholder, except one who has told
-- the corporation in writing that they do not want a copy. The relation: the shareholders are owed the copy; the corporation owes
-- it. The meeting (or signing) day is day 0; sending on or before the twenty-first day before it is in time (fork F-159-before).
-- src:1953 | 159 (1) A corporation shall, not less than twenty-one days before each annual meeting of shareholders or before the signing of a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) in lieu of the annual meeting, send a copy of the documents referred to in section 155 to each shareholder, except to a shareholder who has informed the corporation in writing that he or she does not want a copy of those documents.
@ref CBCA s 159(1) (src:1953)
`the twenty-one days of s 159(1)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 21, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 159(1) (src:1953)
GIVEN `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want a copy of the documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send the documents to the shareholder within s 159(1)` MEANS
    (NOT `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want a copy of the documents`)

@ref CBCA s 159(1) (src:1953)
GIVEN `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to send the documents to the shareholders within s 159(1)` MEANS
    `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` MINUS 21

@ref CBCA s 159(1) (src:1953)
GIVEN `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents were sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the documents were sent in time within s 159(1)` MEANS
    `the date the documents were sent` AT MOST (`the last day to send the documents to the shareholders within s 159(1)` `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it`)

-- (2) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with (1) is guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000;
-- no imprisonment ceiling is stated (NOTHING).
-- src:1955 | (2) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 159(2) (src:1955)
GIVEN `the corporation failed to comply with subsection 159(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 159(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation failed to comply with subsection 159(1)`
    AND `the failure was without reasonable cause`

@ref CBCA s 159(2) (src:1955)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 159(2)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

§§ `s 160 -- copies to the Director`

-- (2) A subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with the section if (a) its holding corporation's financial statements
-- are in consolidated or combined form and include the subsidiary's accounts; and (b) those statements are included in the
-- documents the holding corporation sends to the Director in compliance with the section.
-- src:1961 | (2) A subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with this section if
-- src:1962 | (a) the financial statements of its holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary; and
-- src:1963 | (b) the consolidated or combined financial statements of the holding corporation are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with this section.
@ref CBCA s 160(2) (src:1961-1963)
GIVEN `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with s 160 within s 160(2)` MEANS
        `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary`
    AND `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160`

-- (1) A distributing corporation, any of the issued securities of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person,
-- shall send a copy of the documents of s 155 to the Director (a) not less than twenty-one days before each annual meeting, or
-- without delay after a resolution under s 142(1)(b) is signed; and (b) in any event within fifteen months after the last preceding
-- annual meeting should have been held or a resolution in lieu should have been signed, but no later than six months after the
-- end of the preceding financial year. The relation: the Director is owed the copy; the corporation owes it.
-- src:1957 | 160 (1) A distributing corporation, any of the issued securities of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person, shall send a copy of the documents referred to in section 155 to the Director
-- src:1958 | (a) not less than twenty-one days before each annual meeting of shareholders, or without delay after a resolution referred to in paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed; and
-- src:1959 | (b) in any event within fifteen months after the last preceding annual meeting should have been held or a resolution in lieu of the meeting should have been signed, but no later than six months after the end of the corporation’s preceding financial year.
@ref CBCA s 160(1) (src:1957-1959)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of its issued securities remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons who hold them` IS A NUMBER
      `the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with section 160 under subsection 160(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)` MEANS
        `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
    AND `any of its issued securities remain outstanding`
    AND `the number of persons who hold them` GREATER THAN 1
    AND (NOT `the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with section 160 under subsection 160(2)`)

-- (a) For an annual meeting, the copy is sent on or before the twenty-first day before it; for a resolution in lieu, without delay
-- after it is signed ("without delay" is the caller's judgment).
@ref CBCA s 160(1)(a) (src:1958)
GIVEN `a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed in lieu of the annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the annual meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents were sent to the Director` IS A DATE
      `the documents were sent to the Director without delay after the resolution was signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the documents were sent to the Director in time within s 160(1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed in lieu of the annual meeting`
    THEN `the documents were sent to the Director without delay after the resolution was signed`
    ELSE `the date the documents were sent to the Director` AT MOST (`the date of the annual meeting` MINUS 21)

-- (b) The later limit: within fifteen months after the last preceding annual meeting should have been held (or the resolution
-- in lieu signed), but no later than six months after the end of the preceding financial year. Both apply, so the copy is due
-- by the earlier of the two days (fork F-133-earlier of the meetings module, read the same way here).
-- src:1959 | (b) in any event within fifteen months after the last preceding annual meeting should have been held or a resolution in lieu of the meeting should have been signed, but no later than six months after the end of the corporation’s preceding financial year.
@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b) (src:1959)
`the fifteen months of s 160(1)(b)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b) (src:1959)
`the six months of s 160(1)(b)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b) (src:1959)
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of` `the fifteen months of s 160(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` AT MOST (`the last day of` `the six months of s 160(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`)
    THEN `the last day of` `the fifteen months of s 160(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed`
    ELSE `the last day of` `the six months of s 160(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`

@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b) (src:1959)
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the date the documents were sent to the Director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the documents were sent to the Director in any event in time within s 160(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the date the documents were sent to the Director` AT MOST (`the last day to send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`)

-- (3) A corporation that fails to comply with the section is guilty of an offence, fine not exceeding $5,000; no imprisonment
-- ceiling is stated (NOTHING).
-- src:1965 | (3) A corporation that fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 160(3) (src:1965)
GIVEN `the corporation must send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation failed to comply with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 160(3)` MEANS
        `the corporation must send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)`
    AND `the corporation failed to comply with section 160`

@ref CBCA s 160(3) (src:1965)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 160(3)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING
